

### 19.3. Standard Solutions

These have been chosen to have the asymptotic behavior exhibited in 19.8. The first is Whittaker's function [19.8, 19.9] in a more symmetrical notation.

**19.3.1**

\(U(a,z)\!=\!D_{-a-1}(x)\!=\!\cos\pi(\!1\!+\!\frac{1}{2}a)\!\cdot\!Y_{1}\)

\(-\sin\pi(\!1\!+\!\frac{1}{2}a)\!\cdot\!Y_{2}\)

**19.3.2**

\(V(a,z)\!=\!\frac{1}{\Gamma(\!1\!-\!a\!)}\;\{\sin\pi(\!1\!+\!\frac{1}{2}a)\! \cdot\!Y_{1}\)

\(+\cos\pi(\!1\!+\!\frac{1}{2}a)\!\cdot\!Y_{1}\)

in which

**19.3.3**

\(Y_{1}\!=\!\frac{1}{\sqrt{\pi}}\frac{\Gamma(\frac{1}{2}\!-\!\frac{1}{2}a)}{2^{ \mu+1}\Gamma(\frac{3}{2}\!+\!\frac{1}{2}a)}\,y_{1}\)

**19.3.4**

\(Y_{2}\!=\!\frac{1}{\sqrt{\pi}}\;\frac{\Gamma(\frac{2}{2}\!-\!\frac{1}{2}a)}{2^ {\mu-1}\Gamma}\;y_{2}\!=\!\sqrt{\pi}\;\frac{\cos\pi(\!1\!+\!\frac{1}{2}a)}{2^ {\mu-1}\Gamma(\frac{1}{2}\!+\!\frac{1}{2}a)}\,y_{2}\)

**19.3.5**

\(U(a,0)\!=\!\frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2^{\mu+1}\Gamma(\frac{3}{2}\!+\!\frac{1}{2}a)}\)

\(U^{\prime}(a,0)\!=\!-\frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2^{\mu-1}\Gamma(\frac{1}{2}\!+\!\frac{1 }{2}a)}\)

\(U^{\prime}(a,0)\!=\!-\frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2^{\mu-1}\Gamma(\frac{1}{2}\!+\!\frac{1 }{2}a)}\)

**19.3.6**

\(V(a,0)\!=\!\!\frac{2^{\mu+1}\sin\pi(\frac{3}{2}\!-\!\frac{1}{2}a)}{\Gamma( \frac{3}{2}\!-\!\frac{1}{2}a)}\)

\(V^{\prime}(a,0)\!=\!\!\frac{2^{\mu+1}\sin\pi(\frac{1}{2}\!-\!\frac{1}{2}a)}{ \Gamma(\frac{3}{2}\!-\!\frac{1}{2}a)}\)

In terms of the more familiar \(D_{n}(x)\) of Whittaker,

**19.3.7**

\(U(a,x)\!=\!\!D_{-a-1}(x)\)

**19.3.8**

\(V(a,x)\!=\!\!\frac{1}{\pi}\;\Gamma(\frac{1}{2}\!+\!a)\,\{\sin\pi a\!\cdot\!D_ {-a-1}(x)\!+\!D_{-a-1}(-x)\}\)

**19.4. Wronskian and Other Relations**

**19.4.1**

\(W\,(U,V)\!=\!\sqrt{2/\pi}\)

**19.4.2**

\(\pi V(a,z)\!=\!\Gamma(\frac{1}{2}\!+\!a)\,\{\sin\pi a\!\cdot\!U(a,x)\!+\!U(a, -\!x)\}\)

**19.4.3**

\(\Gamma(\frac{3}{2}\!+\!a)U(a,x)\!=\!\pi\;\sec^{2}\pi a\,\{V(a,-\!x)\}\)

**19.4.4**

\(-\sin\pi a\!\cdot\!V(a,x)\}\)

